  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}\u2061\\theta -{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}\u2061\\theta -({sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}\u2061\\theta -{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}\u2061\\theta -{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta ({tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }({tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1)}{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1 \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1)-1 \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{4}\u2061\\theta -{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }={sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta -2.\n$$",
